            <ArticleTitle>Chest pain with giant global T wave inversions and extreme QT prolongation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>664.e1-664.e2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0735-6757(16)30809-9</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.ajem.2016.11.001</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Negative T waves in electrocardiography have been widely studied. We presents a case of Wellens' syndrome which is a pattern of global inverted T waves with QT prolongation on ECG due to transient proximal LAD occlusion and pointed out other differential diagnosis.</AbstractText>
